# Available Tools in This Container

You are running in a Docker container with full sudo access.

## Pre-installed
- Node.js 22 LTS with npm
- Python 3.12 (system) and uv
- Docker CE with Compose + buildx
- claude CLI (native install, autoupdate disabled)
- git, curl, wget, jq

## Minimal Image
This is the minimal variant — only basic tools are pre-installed.
Install whatever you need with `sudo apt-get install ...`, `npm install -g ...`,
`uv pip install --system ...`, etc.

## Notes
- Passwordless sudo access
- Docker socket may be mounted for docker-in-docker. The workspace path inside
  the container matches the host path, so `docker run -v "$PWD/data:/data"` from
  within resolves correctly on the host.
- `~/.claude/bin` is in PATH — drop custom scripts there.
- `/aicodebox-init.d/*.sh` scripts fire once on first container create.
- Extra host directories may be mounted via `CLAUDEBOX_MOUNT_*` env vars.

## IMPORTANT
If you need to overwrite this CLAUDE.md, first save the container environment
notes above to `~/.claude/CONTAINER.md` so you don't lose the container-specific
context. This file is regenerated on first container create only.
